From da588896785602ad143e02845836f72defca6e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 12:03:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0075 -- v1.0.1 default-flip: L3 + L2b
 default-ON, SB16 FM_VOL 24->28

Why DOS needs this:

The Bug 6 ship config is operator-validated on the DX2-66 (bug6-balance
PLAY3): Lever 3 + Lever 2b + opl3 + auto-RATEDIV (shift_div=2) + CT1745
voice=31/fm=28 = correct SFX pitch, good SFX-vs-music balance, no
stutter, good tempo, clean quit. This patch makes that the OUT-OF-BOX
default so a plain zero-env boot is the validated config.

Dedicated patch-on-patch (NOT in-place edits to the frozen lever
patches 0071/0072/0074) per the codebase default-flip precedent
(0093 default-flip-tier2, 0088 direct-vesa-default-on, 0105
revert-default-flip): keeps the real-HW-validated lever patches intact +
gives a single-revert if v1.0.1 needs to roll back to default-OFF.

Three transforms in SDL_dosaudio_sb.c:

1. L3 gate (0071 resolve): SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX flips from
   strict-"1" (default OFF) to killswitch (default ON; only literal "0"
   disables). The backend-organya gate is UNCHANGED -- L3 is still forced
   OFF under AUDIO_BACKEND=organya (Bug 5 interlock holds at default-ON).
   L3 is a CROSS-SIDE AND: the engine's pixtone_irq_mix_active() ANDs its
   own env parse with SDL_DOSPixtoneIRQMixActive(); nxengine-evo/0170
   flips the engine half. BOTH must flip or L3 stays off -- they're
   coordinated (cross-link-unit lock with nx-engine).

2. L2b gate (0072 resolve): SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MIDI_ISR_TICK flips the
   same way. L2b is ENTIRELY SDL-driven: the engine has no independent
   default and follows SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive() at every site (callback
   register + main-loop-skip + pause/resume), so this single SDL flip is
   the whole L2b default-ON -- register and skip flip together off the one
   query, so the "skip-without-register -> MIDI dies" half-flip is
   structurally impossible. nxengine-evo/0170 has ZERO L2b code.

3. SB16 FM_VOL default (0074 CT1745 block): 24 -> 28 (voice stays 31).
   The operator-validated SFX-vs-music balance from the balance-sweep
   iter. Env-tunable as before; only the compiled default changes.

Banner wording flipped to match: the L3 + L2b ENABLED variants now read
"(default-ON since v1.0.1; set ...=0 to disable; ...)" and the DISABLED
variants read "(killswitch ...=0; ...)". The ENABLED/DISABLED keyword is
preserved so the smoke gate's banner regex still matches; both branches
stay in the code (the =0 regression path).

Smoke gate (tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh, doskutsu repo -- not in this
patch): two NEW required-on-default-boot assertions added --
"audio: SDL/0071 pixtone IRQ-mix: ENABLED" + "audio: SDL/0072 midi tick
from ISR: ENABLED" (severity required) -- so a zero-env smoke FAILS if
the default-flip regresses (or half-flips). The engine 0167/0168 banner
regexes are retargeted to nxengine-evo/0170's new default-ON wording
(kept optional -- engine banners may not fire under DOSBox-X smoke).
BOOT.md L3/L2b/FM_VOL entries updated to default-ON / default-28 + the
=0 killswitch framing.

Byte-identity: v1.0.1's default path is INTENTIONALLY no longer
byte-identical to v1.0.0 -- it's the new ship config. The byte-identical
fallbacks remain: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX=0 (L3 off ->
SDL3_mixer path), SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MIDI_ISR_TICK=0 (L2b off ->
main-loop tick), SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SB16_MIXER_PROGRAM=0 (CT1745
untouched). All killswitches preserved.

DOSBox-X smoke confirms the ENABLED banners / boot path but NOT the
audible pitch / balance / stutter behavior per [[dosbox_not_proxy]];
the all-defaults config validates only on real DX2-66 hardware (the
final all-defaults confirm iter).

Workspace-local per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never upstreamed.

See docs/internal/V1_0_1-DEFAULT-FLIP-AND-FINAL-ITER-DESIGN.md (flush-instr
spec) + bug6_sfx_clip_pitch_mechanism + v1_0_1_rc2_iter_verdict.

